<div id="UsageDescription" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="24" data-tchmi-height="120" data-tchmi-right="24">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">MyControl has the attribute <code style="font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px;">MyAttribute</code> of an object type. Its value is a static object whose properties contain symbol expressions. Every expression uses <code style="font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px;">BindingMode=TwoWay</code>, so MyControl can write changed values back to the symbols. The inputs in the bar below are bound to the same internal symbols, so a change on one side immediately shows up on the other.</p>
</div>
<div id="UsageCode" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="160" data-tchmi-height="228" data-tchmi-width="528">
<pre style="margin: 0; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 16px; overflow: hidden; background: rgba(30, 36, 48, 1); color: rgba(214, 222, 235, 1); border-radius: 4px; font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;">&lt;div id="UsageMyControl"
     data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.MyPackage.MyControl"&gt;
&lt;script
  data-tchmi-target-attribute="data-tchmi-my-attribute"
  type="application/json"&gt;
{
  "number1": "%i%Number1<span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">|BindingMode=TwoWay</span>%/i%",
  "number2": "%i%Number2<span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">|BindingMode=TwoWay</span>%/i%",
  "number3": "%i%Number3<span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">|BindingMode=TwoWay</span>%/i%"
}
&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</pre>
</div>
